 "marca": "COFFEE, BUT WHY?",
 "nota_datos": "Micronicho: el café prohibido. Meca, 1511: Kha'ir Beg vio hombres tomando café fuera de una mezquita y le pareció sospechoso (Atlas Obscura, Taylor & Francis); reunió a eruditos para decidir si prohibirlo (PopSci/Yahoo); cerraron cafés, quemaron granos y golpearon a bebedores (PopSci/Yahoo); el sultán de El Cairo, bebedor de café, lo revirtió (Tasting Table, PopSci); la prohibición no duró ni un año (Atlas Obscura: semanas; Tasting Table). El destino de Kha'ir Beg es discutido: no se menciona. Personajes = ilustración.",
 "frases": [
  "In 1511, an official in Mecca saw men drinking coffee, and he didn't like it.",
  "So he called in scholars to judge one thing: coffee.",
  "The verdict: guilty. Coffee was banned.",
  "Coffeehouses closed. Beans were burned. Drinkers were beaten.",
  "Then the sultan in Cairo heard about it, and he drank coffee himself.",
  "The ban didn't even last a year.",
  "Tell me if you would have hidden your coffee.",
  "Follow for more banned coffee stories."
 ],
